From 53609f87c9971e36369e94fdd6c87e29b7da7a06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pierre-augustin <pierre.augustin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:20:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] audiopolicy: Use the analog dock as the speaker for calls

Speakerphone is selected by setting the device speaker as preferred
device for the phone strategy, which returns it before any routing rule.
On devices whose loudspeaker accessories connect as an analog dock (e.g.
Moto Mods speakers), calls then stay on the phone speaker even while media
plays on the dock, whereas Motorola's stock audio policy routed
speakerphone calls to the dock (the stock audio HAL then uses
mod-voice-speaker and the mod-aware microphone path).

When the speaker is preferred for the phone/DTMF strategies, FOR_DOCK is
FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK and an analog dock is connected, return the dock
instead. FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK is only set when the device opts in (see
config_dockAudioUseAnalogDock), so other devices are not affected.

Not built or tested yet. Expected behavior taken from a Moto Z2 Play on
stock Oreo (same audio_mods HAL), where a speakerphone call goes to output
devices 0x800 and the HAL picks mod-voice-speaker.

Change-Id: I804945e588d4827443aa5b38e9bce9c23ca753a3
---
 services/audiopolicy/enginedefault/src/Engine.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/audiopolicy/enginedefault/src/Engine.cpp b/services/audiopolicy/enginedefault/src/Engine.cpp
index b927cc1..647f43f 100644
--- a/services/audiopolicy/enginedefault/src/Engine.cpp
+++ b/services/audiopolicy/enginedefault/src/Engine.cpp
@@ -830,6 +830,18 @@ DeviceVector Engine::getDevicesForProductStrategy(product_strategy_t strategy) c
     DeviceVector preferredAvailableDevVec =
             getPreferredAvailableDevicesForProductStrategy(availableOutputDevices, strategy);
     if (!preferredAvailableDevVec.isEmpty()) {
+        // When the device speaker is selected for a call and an analog dock audio accessory
+        // (e.g. a Moto Mods speaker) is connected with media routed to it (FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK),
+        // use the dock as the speaker, like Motorola's stock audio policy did.
+        if ((legacyStrategy == STRATEGY_PHONE || legacyStrategy == STRATEGY_DTMF)
+                && getForceUse(AUDIO_POLICY_FORCE_FOR_DOCK) == AUDIO_POLICY_FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK
+                && preferredAvailableDevVec.containsDeviceWithType(AUDIO_DEVICE_OUT_SPEAKER)) {
+            DeviceVector analogDock =
+                    availableOutputDevices.getDevicesFromType(AUDIO_DEVICE_OUT_ANLG_DOCK_HEADSET);
+            if (!analogDock.isEmpty()) {
+                return analogDock;
+            }
+        }
         return preferredAvailableDevVec;
     }
 
